246
00:21:26,172 --> 00:21:28,472
[SPEAKER_08]: Thank you, Suzanne, and good evening, members of the school committee.

247
00:21:28,492 --> 00:21:38,674
[SPEAKER_08]: I don't think we have anybody else from the committee, but I'll talk a little bit about what the policy is and what the requirements are, and sort of the committee that worked together over this past year.

248
00:21:38,694 --> 00:21:45,636
[SPEAKER_08]: So just a little bit of an overview of what the policy is, what it means for our students, our families, our schools.

249
00:21:46,356 --> 00:21:53,017
[SPEAKER_08]: Really, the policy looks at creating a school environment that supports the whole child, looking at student health, nutrition,

250
00:21:53,637 --> 00:22:00,020
[SPEAKER_08]: physical activity, social-emotional well-being, and how closely that is connected to how our students learn and succeed.

251
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:05,243
[SPEAKER_08]: The policy really starts with establishing a district-wide wellness committee.

252
00:22:05,703 --> 00:22:10,065
[SPEAKER_08]: That wellness committee includes the school staff, families, students, community members.

253
00:22:10,085 --> 00:22:19,130
[SPEAKER_08]: I feel like I'm forgetting somebody, but lots of people on our wellness committee, and establishing that that committee meets at least four times a year.

254
00:22:19,910 --> 00:22:22,452
[SPEAKER_08]: So we did establish that committee in this past school year, 25-26.

255
00:22:22,472 --> 00:22:27,394
[SPEAKER_08]: Rhetta Smith, who's the director of food services and I co-chaired that committee.

256
00:22:28,155 --> 00:22:39,201
[SPEAKER_08]: We also had Dr. Sabia, who's our school physician, Stacey Schulman, director of school counseling and behavioral health, Rachel Perry, director of physical education, health education, and countless administrators, staff.

257
00:22:39,281 --> 00:22:42,383
[SPEAKER_08]: I think we had a group of like 25 people in our wellness committee.

258
00:22:42,403 --> 00:22:47,025
[SPEAKER_08]: We also included a couple of students who are going to join us again this year, which is great.

259
00:22:47,045 --> 00:22:48,346
[SPEAKER_08]: So we'll have that continuity.

260
00:22:49,006 --> 00:22:50,687
[SPEAKER_08]: with those students who were with us last year.

261
00:22:50,707 --> 00:22:58,752
[SPEAKER_08]: Establishing that committee and updating the policy is a requirement every three years.

262
00:22:59,353 --> 00:23:03,756
[SPEAKER_08]: And so we probably haven't looked at this in much longer than that.

263
00:23:03,836 --> 00:23:08,779
[SPEAKER_08]: So really our task this last year was really to take a look at this policy.

264
00:23:08,799 --> 00:23:09,899
[SPEAKER_08]: We partnered with

265
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:19,263
[SPEAKER_08]: DESE and the John Stalker Institute with a wellness coach to really walk us through sort of what the regulations say, what's required, what's best practice.

266
00:23:19,823 --> 00:23:25,985
[SPEAKER_08]: And so the majority of what you see when you look through this wellness policy is really what DESE is saying needs to be in this policy.

267
00:23:26,445 --> 00:23:33,928
[SPEAKER_08]: We have a couple of outliers and I'll sort of go over what those are, but we as a committee thought that they were important to include in the policy.

268
00:23:35,822 --> 00:23:40,563
[SPEAKER_08]: Let's see, so what you're looking at when you look at this policy, so there's eight goals.

269
00:23:41,383 --> 00:23:47,665
[SPEAKER_08]: First goal is about implementation, just having a wellness committee, evaluating the policy, what our communication looks like.

270
00:23:48,305 --> 00:23:53,666
[SPEAKER_08]: It's required that we post all of our minutes and agendas on our website and things like that.

271
00:23:54,526 --> 00:24:01,068
[SPEAKER_08]: It also establishes the standards for nutrition and accessible meals, looks at the USDA standards and competitive foods.

272
00:24:02,212 --> 00:24:16,654
[SPEAKER_08]: encourages physical activity and physical education in our schools, looks at nutrition, education and food literacy, addresses food allergies and other food related practices in our schools, supports social emotional health and also support staff wellness.

273
00:24:18,269 --> 00:24:25,373
[SPEAKER_08]: really overall this policy is looking at the fact that healthy students are in a better position to learn, participate and thrive in our schools.

274
00:24:25,393 --> 00:24:35,560
[SPEAKER_08]: And that's really what we're doing with this policy and really creating an environment that allows students to make those healthy choices every day and be supported in making those healthy choices.

275
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:43,965
[SPEAKER_08]: So I don't know, I was trying to remember if we've done a reading of this policy yet and maybe someone can tell me if we have or not.

