483
00:43:44,073 --> 00:43:44,333
[SPEAKER_07]: Thank you.

484
00:43:45,314 --> 00:43:53,538
[SPEAKER_07]: This here is a brief cartoon diagram that I'm about to describe is what the new systems will be.

485
00:43:54,959 --> 00:44:02,022
[SPEAKER_07]: Because of the electrification, we're limited to either air source or water source type of technology.

486
00:44:02,042 --> 00:44:12,247
[SPEAKER_07]: What we're going to try to do is we are going to use high efficiency systems to draw heating and cooling from outside air.

487
00:44:13,287 --> 00:44:18,011
[SPEAKER_07]: And that is why these are these machines are called air to water heat pump.

488
00:44:18,151 --> 00:44:25,477
[SPEAKER_07]: So if you look at the diagram on the top left corner of the diagram, that's just a symbolic diagram of what they generally look like.

489
00:44:25,537 --> 00:44:30,941
[SPEAKER_07]: They're essentially chillers, but they have refrigerant systems or

490
00:44:33,323 --> 00:44:37,387
[SPEAKER_07]: cycles in them that are reversible, so they can do cooling and heating.

491
00:44:38,609 --> 00:44:49,100
[SPEAKER_07]: And like I said, the source is air, so the electric connection gets to these units and then they produce heating and cooling depending on the time of the year.

492
00:44:49,640 --> 00:44:52,701
[SPEAKER_07]: They are capable of simultaneous heating and cooling as well.

493
00:44:53,382 --> 00:44:57,784
[SPEAKER_07]: So essentially, this becomes your primary source of heating and cooling for the building.

494
00:44:57,884 --> 00:45:08,609
[SPEAKER_07]: So whatever we're doing for ventilation in the building or air conditioning of sorts, this is what we're going to use to produce energy and bring it into the building.

495
00:45:11,149 --> 00:45:22,792
[SPEAKER_07]: The other parts of the improvements in the project also include a replacement of existing boilers with all-electric boilers.

496
00:45:24,252 --> 00:45:31,254
[SPEAKER_07]: Primarily, we have to have those because there is a slight limitation into the modern air-to-water source heat pumps.

497
00:45:31,314 --> 00:45:36,435
[SPEAKER_07]: They do start to go into defrost cycles once the ambient temperatures are below 40 degrees.

498
00:45:38,675 --> 00:45:47,660
[SPEAKER_07]: especially in humid days, and they also tend to degrade quite a bit by the time the ambient temperatures get to zero degrees.

499
00:45:48,020 --> 00:46:00,025
[SPEAKER_07]: However, current modern code requires us to design these systems to 100% of the capacity of the required ambient temperatures for our building.

500
00:46:00,265 --> 00:46:03,367
[SPEAKER_07]: And here in Medford, that design temperature is 7.7 degrees.

501
00:46:05,868 --> 00:46:18,818
[SPEAKER_07]: So our targeted sizing of this piece of equipment is that at 7 degrees, we will be able to provide 100% of the heating required for the building.

502
00:46:18,899 --> 00:46:22,762
[SPEAKER_07]: And on the cooling side, it will be designed for 95 degrees, somewhere around there.

503
00:46:24,747 --> 00:46:35,091
[SPEAKER_07]: Once the temperatures do drop below those ambient conditions, especially below zero, we would need to use the electric boilers as a backup.

504
00:46:36,091 --> 00:46:48,575
[SPEAKER_07]: And the controls will be set up in a way that we don't allow electric boilers to operate unless there is something wrong with the equipment or it's not operating as it should.

505
00:46:49,935 --> 00:47:00,519
[SPEAKER_07]: And, you know, there will be a pretty robust control system that will look at equipment, you know, troubleshooting and trouble codes.

506
00:47:02,440 --> 00:47:10,543
[SPEAKER_07]: The other part of the improvements for the building is that we are replacing certain components of the air handling units.

507
00:47:11,223 --> 00:47:14,445
[SPEAKER_07]: Two out of three units were constant airflow systems.

508
00:47:14,645 --> 00:47:18,006
[SPEAKER_07]: We are converting them to variable airflow systems by adding

509
00:47:18,886 --> 00:47:24,028
[SPEAKER_07]: variable frequency drives to them to get the best efficiency out of these units.

510
00:47:25,088 --> 00:47:36,973
[SPEAKER_07]: We're also replacing existing coils that are within the air handling units so that we can temper the air through water, low water temperature instead of refrigerant.

511
00:47:38,834 --> 00:47:58,307
[SPEAKER_07]: And then other parts of the improvements include replacing unit ventilators that exist in every classroom, like I said, and the idea there is that we will replace them in kind with the most modern unit ventilators and that they are going to use the existing louvers that exist.

512
00:48:00,189 --> 00:48:15,597
[SPEAKER_07]: Other pieces of equipment that we will be improving on will be the following, but not limited to those, the radiators, cabinet unit heaters, propeller unit heaters, variable air volume boxes, and then any duct modded heating coils.

