951
01:27:46,994 --> 01:27:58,839
[SPEAKER_05]: Resolution in support of e-bike safety education, whereas Metro Public Schools wishes to encourage safe active transportation to and from school, defined here as human power mobility, such as biking or walking.

952
01:27:59,540 --> 01:28:09,424
[SPEAKER_05]: Whereas the Commonwealth Special Commission on Micromobility January 2026 report, cities statewide increases in e-bike scooter and e-motor.

953
01:28:10,653 --> 01:28:20,577
[SPEAKER_05]: commuting an estimated 23% annual increase in related injuries since 2017, with more than one third of those injuries occurring in children 14 and under.

954
01:28:20,597 --> 01:28:29,681
[SPEAKER_05]: Whereas Massachusetts Safe Routes to School Program has created resources for schools to educate students and community members in matters of pedestrian, bike and e-bike safety.

955
01:28:29,701 --> 01:28:37,564
[SPEAKER_05]: Now therefore be it resolved that the Medford Public Schools will provide students, families and staff with educational information about laws,

956
01:28:38,045 --> 01:28:44,307
[SPEAKER_05]: regulations and recommended safety practices for bikes, e-bikes and other micromobility devices within the first month of school.

957
01:28:45,168 --> 01:28:45,768
[SPEAKER_05]: Good resolution.

958
01:28:45,808 --> 01:28:47,708
[SPEAKER_05]: Thank you, Member Reinfeldt, and I'll turn it over to you.

959
01:28:48,869 --> 01:28:51,110
[SPEAKER_06]: Again, I hope this is self-explanatory.

960
01:28:51,230 --> 01:28:57,372
[SPEAKER_06]: We're seeing an increase in these e-bikes and commuting and students are

961
01:28:59,287 --> 01:29:12,193
[SPEAKER_06]: could use some education around the actual rules for what is an e-bike, what is an e-moto, and just generally there's information out there and this is providing one more way of getting this to students.

962
01:29:12,333 --> 01:29:17,836
[SPEAKER_06]: I actually wrote this resolution before I saw last week's memo, which included some of this already.

963
01:29:17,916 --> 01:29:26,020
[SPEAKER_06]: So I think this is really well aligned with what the district is doing, but to formalize the fact that we want students and staff and families to be educated about

964
01:29:26,820 --> 01:29:30,621
[SPEAKER_06]: the different transportation options and the safety requirements around that.

965
01:29:30,721 --> 01:29:35,302
[SPEAKER_06]: No more kids riding around with no helmets or helmets unbuckled, all of that.

966
01:29:36,242 --> 01:29:38,163
[SPEAKER_06]: We should be supporting safe behaviors.

967
01:29:38,703 --> 01:29:39,223
[SPEAKER_06]: Motion to approve.

968
01:29:40,003 --> 01:29:40,243
[SPEAKER_05]: Yes.

969
01:29:40,443 --> 01:29:43,664
[SPEAKER_05]: Helmets are required for, I think, 16 and under, so by law.

970
01:29:44,224 --> 01:29:44,964
[SPEAKER_05]: Yep, so by law.

971
01:29:45,024 --> 01:29:47,605
[SPEAKER_06]: And e-motos are not allowed 16 and below.

972
01:29:47,645 --> 01:29:49,985
[SPEAKER_06]: It is considered a motor vehicle, things like that.

